<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53627" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστανικαί</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Gal.
			6.777
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			791
		</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστηνοῦ</span></b>  (gen. sg.)
			<i><span class="en">
			Nic.
			<u>Al.</u>
			269
		</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καστανέα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chestnut-tree,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gp.
				2.8.4
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάστανος</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρύαι</span>
			; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάστανον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				10.63.1
			</span></i>; derived by the ancients from <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καστανέα</span></b> , a place in Asia Minor (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις Μαγνησίας</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				493.26
			</span></i> (cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καστανὶς</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἶα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					271
				</span></i>
			); but cf. Armen. <i>kask</i>: for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρυον</span></div>
